[[Category:Tmp_xyobj(neg)]]

'''Foxes''' are neutral [[creatures]] commonly encountered almost anywhere in the Hearthlands. They are an accessible source of [[Raw Fox|meat]], [[Raw Fox Hide|hide]], and [[Fox#Production|more]].

== Acquisition ==
Foxes spawn individually as entities in all [[forest]] and [[grassland]] [[terrain]] at all times of year. In addition to this, they can be found in significant numbers within [[Fox Hole|Fox Holes]].

Dispatched foxes can be skinned, cleaned, and butchered via right click by [[Hearthling|Hearthlings]] that have learned [[Hunting]]. While fox corpses cannot be placed in a Hearthling's [[inventory]], they can be lifted and stored within objects such as [[Cart|Carts]] and [[Shed|Sheds]].

The [[quality]] of a dispatched fox is calculated upon death, and its total is hardcapped by both a Hearthling's [[Survival]] and the quality of any [[Weapons|weapon]] or [[Sharp Tool|sharp tool]] used to kill them.

== Behavior ==
Foxes are neutral until attacked, at which point they will initiate [[combat]] and give chase. Foxes run at above Hearthling run speed, so a Hearthling must be sprinting, riding a vehicle, or on [[Horse|horseback]] to outrun or give chase.

Foxes will hunt small game such as [[Squirrel|squirrels]] and [[Rabbit|rabbits]], and will attack any Hearthling that disrupts a chase by stealing their prey. Foxes are themselves hunted by [[Badger|badgers]] and [[Wolverine|wolverines]], which will chase, attack, and inevitably overpower the fox, leaving its corpse to be freely obtained by any nearby Hearthling.

=== Combat ===
Because foxes do not attack nor defend often, cannot utilize {{RoB color|oppressive|Oppressive}} Openings, and can be comfortably outrun on grassland terrain, they make an approachable target for any fledgling hunter attempting to gain combat experience. Although they are not particularly strong, a minimum of 15 in relevant combat [[Attributes]] is recommended.

